# Cursor Rules for EPSRC Small Grants Application

## Language and Spelling

**CRITICAL: Use UK English spelling throughout all documents.**

When editing, creating, or suggesting text for this grant application, always use UK English spelling conventions. Examples:

- **-ise/-isation** endings (not -ize/-ization): analyse, organise, optimise, specialise, recognise, organisation, optimisation, specialisation
- **-our** endings (not -or): colour, behaviour, favour, honour, labour
- **-re** endings (not -er): centre, theatre, metre, fibre
- **-ogue** endings (not -og): dialogue, catalogue, analogue
- **-ence** endings (not -ense): defence, licence (noun), offence
- **-ll-** in certain words: travelling, cancelled, labelled
- **-ae/-oe** spellings: encyclopaedia, manoeuvre, oestrogen

Common UK vs US differences:
- UK: realise, recognise, optimise, analyse, organise, specialise
- US: realize, recognize, optimize, analyze, organize, specialize

Always default to UK English spelling when in doubt. This applies to all markdown files, documentation, and any text generated for this application.

## Project Context

This is an EPSRC Mathematical Sciences Small Grants application for:
- **Project**: Multi-Scale Persistent Homology for Spatial Multi-Agent Systems
- **Duration**: 12 months
- **Scope**: Full Championship season analysis (~540 games)
- **Timeline**: PI analyzes 15-20 games (Months 1-3), RA analyzes remaining games (Months 4-9), PI coordinates final analysis (Months 10-12)

## Document Structure

Key documents follow numbered naming convention:
- 00_Application_Header.md
- 01_Application_Summary.md
- 02_Vision_and_Approach.md (or V&A R3.md)
- 03_Applicant_and_Team_Capability.md
- 04_References.md
- 05_Project_Partners.md
- 06_Resources_and_Costs_R3.md
- 07_Ethics_and_Responsible_Innovation.md
- 08_Data_Management_Plan.md

## Style Guidelines

- Use formal academic tone appropriate for UKRI grant applications
- Be precise and specific with technical terminology
- Maintain consistency with existing document terminology
- Follow UKRI/EPSRC formatting requirements
